WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.980
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.360
Thanks for coming along.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.330
When I go shopping on my own,
I'm always satisfied with just looking.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.440
I know what you mean.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.400
I'm the same when I go by myself.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.580
Want to stop somewhere for a snack?

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:16.780
Good idea.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.040
Where should we go?

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.800
What's around here?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.160
There's a new burger place.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.300
Have you been there?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.210
This says their shakes are amazing!

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.660
Sensei...

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.780
Did you hear about Inuzuka-sensei?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.990
He lost his wife last year.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:43.960
Really?

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:51.940
Kotori?

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:53.920
What's wrong?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.490
Oh, it's nothing.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:02.170
<i>The Chuo Line rapid train for Takao 
will soon be arriving on track 12.</i>

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.110
<i>The Chuo Line rapid train for Takao 
will soon be arriving on track 12.</i>

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.770
<i>For your safety, please stand 
behind the yellow line.</i>

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.960
It's already been a year...

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.210
<i>Please stand behind the yellow line.</i>

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:46.520
<b>Okonomiyaki Filled With Affection</b>

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.730
<b>Megumi</b>

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.400
I wonder if Sensei and 
Tsumugi-chan have eaten yet.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.560
Oops, sorry.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.130
It's this late already?

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.020
You must be hungry.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:16.790
What should we eat?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.970
I dunno...

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.150
What should we eat?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.440
Tsumugi-san.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.160
Daddy's a little tired today.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.820
Mind if we go out to eat?

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.980
Sure!

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.550
We haven't gone out to eat in forever!

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.840
We haven't?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.310
You've been doing all the cooking.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:44.890
Even at Kotori-chan's place!

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.120
That's right.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:49.240
A family restaurant?

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.040
<b>Ramen</b>

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.040
Let me see...

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.000
Pasta Atelier

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.000
Where would be good?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.630
This place smells really good!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.090
<b>Okonomiyaki Yocchan</b>

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.090
Okonomiyaki?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.010
What's okonomiyaki?

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.240
Oh, right.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.820
We've never had that at home, have we?

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.520
What is it? Is that when you yaki okonomi?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.980
Well, you mix your favorite fillings 
with a tasty flour batter...

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.240
Fillings?

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.770
Like meat, or squid, or shrimp.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.960
You mix it all up yourself,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.870
and cook it on a sizzling hot grill!

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.240
I think I can do that!

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.560
Okay, let's go inside, then.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.370
Okay!

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.110
Welcome.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.880
This way, please.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.600
Is this where it sizzles?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.920
That's right.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.330
I can't wait!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.560
Tsumugi-san, that's dangerous.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.100
I hope it comes soon!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.400
Don't you, Daddy?

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.810
Yeah.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.440
Here you go!

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.310
It's here!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:01.280
Here's your pork and squid okonomiyaki.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:06.890
Mixing...

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:10.410
Oh, they mix it for you here.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.540
What about the mixing and 
making it sizzle yourself?

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:18.260
Oh, the people who work here did it for us.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.500
Doesn't it look good?

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:23.910
What's wrong?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.400
Daddy tricked me!

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.750
Hey, that's mean.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.260
I just didn't know.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.870
But I could do it by myself!

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:34.770
Right, right.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.140
Here, want some seaweed flakes?

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.770
Yes!

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.500
Hey, that's too much!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:44.320
It's fine!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.400
I'll do it myself!

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.120
Tsumugi, stop playing!

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.700
Oh, look. Now you've done it.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.870
Jeez...

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.210
But... Daddy...

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.080
Wait, wait! No crying!

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.800
I'll swap yours with mine.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:05.760
Eat up.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.840
Hey, Tsumugi!

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.990
Shh! Shh!

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.270
No!

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.680
Here, eat this!

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.340
Come on, Tsumugi, let's eat!

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.900
No! No!

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.900
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.190
<b>Okonomiyaki Yocchan</b>

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.190
Thank you very much.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.290
We didn't get to eat much, huh?

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.370
Good morning!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.710
Inuzuka-san, good morning!

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.390
Good morning.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.770
Here she is.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.870
Good morning, Tsumugi-chan!

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.130
Good morning.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.160
Huh?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.940
You seem kind of down.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.140
I'm fine.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.220
Bye!

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.990
Um... Actually,

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.300
my mom has some free time next week,

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.280
and she wants to join us...

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:18.030
Sensei?

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:21.140
Oh, sorry. She wants to have 
a meal with us, right?

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.220
Are you okay?

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.820
Well, not exactly...

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:29.500
I had a fight with Tsumugi last night.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.070
A fight?

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.960
But why?

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.680
Well, you see...

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.930
I see.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.660
I didn't mean to yell.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.080
And when she cried, I panicked.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.610
Then why don't we make okonomiyaki 
when we meet up to cook again?

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.360
Okonomiyaki?

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.880
Let's do it!

00:07:55.880 --> 00:08:00.070
It would be sad if that was her 
first memory of okonomiyaki.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.710
That's true...

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.000
Let's restore your honor!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.790
I wonder if she'll agree to it.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.010
Tsumugi, how was school today?

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.510
It was fun.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.440
Yuuka-chan says

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.900
her mom is nice and doesn't get mad.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:32.840
Mikio-kun's mom is really scary 
because she gets mad.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.120
I don't get mad for no reason,

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.990
but I'll scold you when you 
do something wrong.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.450
Okay.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.370
But I wanted to make it sizzle...

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:47.600
Oh, right!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.460
Next time we meet up to cook together,
we're thinking of making okonomiyaki.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.480
Um, Iida-san...

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:59.660
That's Kotori-san's mom... and 
Kojika Shinobu-san will be there, too.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.720
Kotori-chan's mom!

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.640
Yeah. I'll be meeting her for the first time, too.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.880
I can't wait!

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.830
We're here!

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.730
Tsumu-Tsumu!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.170
Shinobu-chan! I missed you!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:30.460
Hello.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.960
Hello, Sensei.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.060
Thank you for joining us again today.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.340
Wh-What's wrong?

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.310
I'm sorry. My mom...

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.850
had to leave for work again.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.320
I see...

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.660
Really?

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:50.980
Yagi-chan!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.860
I came because I heard she'd be here today.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.320
Sorry, Kotori.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.070
I leaked him the information.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.320
I'm sorry.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.500
Bye, then.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.290
Don't say that!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.830
Yagi-chan, cook with us!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.550
<b>Nozaki</b>

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.250
So, what, it's okonomiyaki this time?

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.550
Yes. I have the ingredients here.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:18.010
<b>Weak Flour</b>

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.010
It's pork and squid okonomiyaki.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.130
All right.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.980
You guys make the pork and squid one, then.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.850
We'll make our own version.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:26.600
Okay.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.360
"We"? You mean us?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.560
That's right.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.980
Come on, let's do it.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.640
First, you make and chill the stock...

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:38.240
Stock?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.860
But I've already chilled this.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:41.830
Okay.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.030
Sieve the weak flour into a bowl,

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.350
and mix it with the stock little by 
little so that it doesn't clump.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:49.400
Okay.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.380
So that it doesn't clump...

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.080
Tsumugi!

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.150
You cast a spell before to keep 
food from clumping, right?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.820
Can you do that again?

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.940
What's that?

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:02.470
I wanna see! How do you do it?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.880
Um...

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:08.160
Like this! Like this, right?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:12.190
Clump, clump! No clumping!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.770
No clumps! Clump, clump, clump!

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:18.330
What is that?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.570
It's the clump-clump dance!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.350
I'll use it on yours!

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:23.550
No, thanks.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.160
Mine's not going to clump.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.100
Hey, Tsumugi, um... Can you do the rest?

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.850
I'm gonna go talk to Yagi-chan.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:32.460
Okay...

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:33.360
See?

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.170
Clump, clump! No clumping!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.170
We don't need that. Go back to your dad.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.380
No!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.920
I want to watch you and Shinobu-chan make it!

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.160
We're fine on our own.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.390
No!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.940
O-Once we grate and mix in the Chinese yam,

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.240
we'll let the batter rest for a bit.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.820
You handle the cabbage, please.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:52.980
Oh, right.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.870
You're a lot faster at cutting now, Sensei.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:00.760
Yeah.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.660
I've gotten better.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.540
You're good, Yagi-chan!

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.450
Watch out. Your face is too close.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:11.040
I'm okay! Keep going!

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.810
Hurry!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.110
I-It kind of makes you lonely, huh?

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.900
Well... It's fun to watch people

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.920
who are really good at it.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.340
What about you? Are you okay?

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.170
You said your mom can't come.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.770
I haven't formally introduced 
myself to her, either.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.350
I know she's busy,

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:41.790
and her job is important. Yeah.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.280
It's just, well...

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:48.400
I wish she would've told me sooner

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.810
that she couldn't come today.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:55.040
It kind of made me feel 
like I don't matter to her.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:13:00.330
Wow, that sounds really childish 
when I say it out loud.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.800
No... My ears are burning.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:11.180
I'm sure it's not that you 
don't matter to your mom.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.560
She probably just had too much on her mind.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.250
Sensei?

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.410
Is something wrong?

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:25.320
Oh, no.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:30.450
It's hard to say, and to show,

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.400
that you're always thinking about someone.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.660
I can do it, too!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:38.700
I don't need your help.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.070
I wanna do it!

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:45.420
Well, I guess they say kids never 
realize how much their parents care.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:48.300
But I think that's okay.

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:51.130
Maybe it's better that they don't.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:57.350
It wouldn't be good for them to realize 
too much and end up worrying about it.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.650
Like you do.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:05.280
Th-That... That's not a compliment.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.050
It is! It is!

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.200
That was dangerous!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.780
Oh, man...

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.440
You're in the way.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.150
Go someplace else.

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:18.470
Tsumugi!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.380
Tsumu-Tsumu's foot hit the bowl.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.170
It's fine, it's fine. We can just wash it off.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:28.960
Tsumugi.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.550
Where's your apology?

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.020
Sorry.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:40.980
Tsumugi, come here.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.010
Tsumugi, do you not like it 
when people scold you?

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:54.500
Yeah.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.420
Daddy doesn't like scolding you, either.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.190
You don't?

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.210
That's right.

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:11.120
But you know you did something 
wrong just now, right?

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:11.930
Uh-huh...

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.240
Remember what I said?

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.970
When you do something wrong, I'll scold you.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.880
You don't like it when 
someone scolds you,

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:23.190
and I don't like scolding you.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.250
But when you do something wrong,

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:27.440
I'll do my best to scold you.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:34.840
You don't like scolding me, either?

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.210
But at the okonomiyaki place,

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.730
I didn't do a good job of scolding you.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.210
A good job?

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:47.650
Yeah.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.010
I didn't do a good job.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.300
I'm sorry.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.680
I'm sorry, too!

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.540
Yeah.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.660
Yagi-chan, I'm sorry!

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:08.320
Sure.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.440
Go help your dad.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:11.260
Okay!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.030
Get to it, Tsumugi!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.420
Leave it to me!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:22.040
Mix, mix, miiiiix!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.740
Come together, mix-ix!

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.500
You sing too, Daddy!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.750
Okay!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.120
Mix, mix, miiiiix!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.930
You join in too, Kotori-chan!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.590
Huh?

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:37.800
All right.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:41.810
Mix, mix, miiiiix!

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:45.810
Come together, mix-ix!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.820
Mix, mix, miiiiix!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:53.830
Come together, mix-ix!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.330
Sizzly!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.500
Now lay the pork belly on top...

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.080
Sizzle! Sizzle!

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.250
Grilly-grill!

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:08.250
And once you turn it over...

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.710
Put the lid on,

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:13.840
then flip it one last time, and...

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.800
It's done!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.600
Spread plenty of sauce on top,

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.810
then add some mayonnaise...

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.480
And lastly, use this...

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.550
to make lines!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.230
I'll do that, too!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:34.330
I wanna try!

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:36.460
Okay, Tsumugi-chan,

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.090
you take care of the rest.

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:38.820
Okay!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.080
It's done!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.000
It looks so good!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.020
We've got the next one cooking, 
so you can go ahead and eat.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:54.240
We can?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.770
Eat it while it's hot.

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:03.350
D-Did I make it?

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:05.050
Mom!

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:06.980
"Mom"?

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.550
Welcome, everyone!

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:10.620
Hello!

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.480
Sorry I'm late.

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:16.870
Inuzuka-sensei, yes?

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:18.400
Yes!

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.680
I want to thank you for always letting me...

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:24.560
No, no, you always do so much for my daughter.

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.620
No, your daughter does so much for me.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.880
Um, I apologize for the late introduction.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.330
I'm Inuzuka.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.920
Not at all. It's my pleasure.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:36.300
I'm Iida Kotori's mother.

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.350
Iida Megumi.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.630
It's really her.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.350
Fanboy.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.760
You're Tsumugi-chan, huh?

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.320
Nice to meet you.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:47.130
Kotori-chan's mommy...

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.280
Hello.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.360
I am Inuzuka Tsumugi.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.450
Thanks for being friends with Kotori.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:57.320
Uh-huh...

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.740
What happened, Mom?

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.900
Work ended early.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.250
I'm sorry for just leaving this morning.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:12.000
I'm late, but is it okay if I join you?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:16.300
Yeah.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:21.670
Okay, I'll get the other room ready.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:25.610
Mom, that outfit!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.470
I was in a hurry, so I'm still in my uniform.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:33.610
I'll go change!

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:35.900
Okay, cheers!

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.200
Cheers!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.370
Which one should I try first?

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:49.440
This is the one Yagi-chin made, 
with beef sinew in it.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:52.290
And Kotori's mom put mushrooms in this one.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:57.500
Let's start with the pork and 
squid one you helped with.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.060
Pork and squid!

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.930
Let's eat!

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.630
It's good!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.820
Why? Why? It's better than the 
one I had at the restaurant!

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.280
Really?

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.860
You're not just saying that?

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:30.290
But it really is good.

00:20:30.610 --> 00:20:32.180
Why? Why?

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.900
Do you want to know?

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.000
Yeah!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:38.970
The reason your dad's okonomiyaki 
tastes so good is...

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:45.220
because he filled it with his affection for you!

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:48.640
Huh?

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.400
That's Kotori's mom for you. 
She said that like it was nothing.

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:54.190
Yeah.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.490
But she's right.

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:58.900
I get it!

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:01.900
Is affection like love?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.210
Huh?

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:04.860
I see!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.370
So that's why it's so good!

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:12.100
Um, listen... Tsumugi-san...

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.580
I eat lots of that, then, huh?

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.210
I see...

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:30.260
You're eating it, Tsumugi?

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:31.510
Yup!

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:36.120
Tsumugi-chan, keep eating good food!

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:36.780
Okay!

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:47.660
It's good, huh?

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:50.030
It's good!
